          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Approximate heights are: A. (+1500) m B. (-500) m C. (+300) m D. (-1200) m E. (+1200) m F. (-200) m G. (+100) m"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.469,
            0.882,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.2. Which is the highest point in this geographical cross-section? Which is the lowest point?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.513,
            0.529,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Highest point is A & the lowest point is D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.54,
            0.881,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.3. Can you write the points A, B, …., G in a sequence of decreasing order of heights? Can you write the point in a sequence of increasing order of heights?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.585,
            0.506,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. A, E, C, G, F, B, D. (Decreasing order) D, B, F, G, C, E, A. (Increasing order)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.639,
            0.769,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.4. What is the highest point above sea level on Earth? What is its height?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.667,
            0.603,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Mount-Everest. Its height above sea level is 8848m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.694,
            0.881,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.5. What is the lowest point with respect to sea level on land or on the ocean floor? What is its height? (This height should be negative).",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.739,
            0.881,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. The lowest know point on the Earth is the challenger deep, located in the Mariana trench in the Pacific Ocean. Its depth is approximately -10994 m."
            }
          ]
        },
